# Netlify SPA fallback.
#
# App.jsx routes with BrowserRouter, so /contact, /products/e-learning and the
# rest exist only once React has booted. The build emits a single index.html and
# no file at any of those paths, so without this rule Netlify answers a direct
# visit, a refresh or a shared link with its own 404 page — the routes work only
# when reached by in-app navigation, which is exactly the case nobody tests.
#
# 200 rather than 301: serve index.html at the requested URL instead of
# redirecting to /, so React Router still sees the real path and renders the
# right page.
/*  /index.html  200
